  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "建模與模擬",
    "sub_ename": "MODELING AND SIMULATION",
    "describe_ch": "本課程介紹建模與模擬，旨在幫助學生理解數學建模與模擬在解決現實問題的重要性，從而激發學生培養對現實問題進行建模、使用程式語言求解模擬模型、並解釋仿真結果之能力。為了實現上述目標，本課程涵蓋以下主題：隨機數的生成、逆變換方法、接受拒絕方法、隨機變數的模擬、蒙特卡羅模擬、模擬模型的範例（選自馬可夫鏈、排隊系統、庫存系統、決策問題與隨機漫步）、模擬模型的驗證與確認、模擬結果的解釋、連續時間系統的模擬模型、常微分方程、動態系統、參數估計、Nelder Mead 單形法、bootstrapping法、馬爾可夫鏈蒙特卡羅方法、SIR 模型、成長模型和機器人最短路徑模型。本課程使用matlab或python程式語言進行模擬。",
    "describe_eh": "This course provides an introduction to modeling and simulation, aiming to help students understand the importance of mathematical modeling and simulation in solving the real-world problems and thus to motivate the students to develop the ability to model the real-world problems, solve the simulation model using programming languages, and interpret the simulation results. To achieve the above objectives, this course covers the following topics: the generation of random numbers, inverse transform method, acceptance and rejection method, simulation of random variables, Monte Carlo simulation, examples of simulation models (selected examples from Markov chains, queueing systems, inventory systems, decision making problems, and random walks), verification and validation of simulation models, interpretation of simulated results, simulation models for continuous-time systems, ordinary differential equations, dynamical systems, parameter estimation, Nelder Mead simplex method, bootstrapping method, Markov Chain Monte Carlo method, SIR models, growth models, and robot shortest path models. The matlab or python programming language is used for simulation in this course.",
    "pre_subname": "",
